{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5413) from a code generation pipeline for the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement `cmd/sleep` covering srd061 requirements R1.1-R1.4 (Core sleep behavior). Specifically:\n   - Create `cmd/sleep/main.go` with the sleep implementation\n   - Create `cmd/sleep/sleep_test.go` with differential tests against the GNU `gsleep` reference binary\n   - The implementation must support: single numeric argument sleep (R1.1), fractional seconds (R1.2), suffix multipliers s/m/h/d (R1.3), and summing multiple arguments (R1.4)\n   - Must pass compilation, go vet, and differential tests\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing**: Compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gsleep` from Homebrew coreutils) using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: All cmd/ utilities must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - **Graceful skip**: Tests must use `exec.LookPath(\"gsleep\")` and `t.Skip` if reference binary not found\n   - **Duration parsing**: Support fractional seconds and suffix multipliers (s=1, m=60, h=3600, d=86400), case-sensitive lowercase only\n   - **Multiple argument summing**: When multiple args given, sum all durations\n   - **Go module**: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n   - **Build pattern**: `go build -o bin/sleep ./cmd/sleep/`\n   - **Copyright header**: Required on all Go files (SPDX MIT license, 2026 Petar Djukic)\n   - **No git commands**: Git is managed externally by the orchestrator\n   - **Write-first strategy**: Write all source files before running any build/test commands\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd061-sleep.yaml** (READ)\n     - This is the SRD defining all requirements for the sleep utility\n     - R1 (Core sleep behavior): R1.1 (single numeric arg), R1.2 (fractional seconds), R1.3 (suffix multipliers s/m/h/d), R1.4 (sum multiple args)\n     - R2 (Input validation): R2.1 (zero duration OK), R2.2 (no args = error), R2.3 (non-numeric = error), R2.4 (infinity/inf support)\n     - R3 (Signal handling): R3.1 (no stdout/stderr output), R3.2 (no stdin), R3.3 (--help), R3.4 (--version)\n     - R4 (Exit codes): R4.1 (exit 0 on success), R4.2 (exit 1 on invalid args), R4.3-R4.4 (differential test requirements)\n     - non_goals: No SIGALRM wake, no remaining time reporting on interruption\n\n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (provided in context)\n     - Pattern to follow: `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` creates buffered channel, signal.Notify for SIGPIPE, goroutine exits 0\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() { <-c; os.Exit(0) }()\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (provided in context)\n     - DiffTest struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles fields\n     - RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests) runs each test as subtest\n     - Harness sets LC_ALL=C by default\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/build.go** (provided in context)\n     - BuildBinary(t, \".\") compiles the cmd/ package and returns binary path\n\n   - **cmd/sleep/main.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Must implement sleep with R1.1-R1.4 requirements\n     - Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at start\n     - Parse duration args with fractional support and suffix multipliers\n     - Sum multiple arguments\n\n   - **cmd/sleep/sleep_test.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests using testutils.BuildBinary and RunDiffTests\n     - LookPath(\"gsleep\") with t.Skip fallback\n     - Test cases: zero duration, fractional seconds, suffixes, multiple args, error cases\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — no code has been written or compiled.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full scope of requirements\n   - The task is scoped to R1.1-R1.4 but a working utility also needs basic error handling (R2.2 for no args, R2.3 for invalid args) to produce meaningful differential test results\n   - Tests should use very short durations (0 or 0.01) per R4.3 to avoid slow test execution\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The first user message is the massive task description containing: role definition, repository_files listing, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task definition, constraints, description with required_reading/files/requirements/design_decisions/acceptance_criteria, shared_protocols, and package_contracts.\n   - The second user message is \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" requesting this summary.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/sleep/main.go` implementing srd061 R1.1-R1.4 (core sleep behavior: single arg, fractional seconds, suffix multipliers, multiple arg summing)\n   - Create `cmd/sleep/sleep_test.go` with differential tests against gsleep\n   - Run `go build -o bin/sleep ./cmd/sleep/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/sleep/...` to verify no issues (AC2)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/sleep/... -count=1` to verify differential tests pass (AC3) or skip gracefully (AC4)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd061-sleep.yaml`) and was about to implement the two files. The SRD read was the only action taken. No code has been written yet. The implementation plan was being formed:\n   \n   For `cmd/sleep/main.go`:\n   - Copyright header, package main\n   - Import sys package for SIGPIPE handler\n   - Parse arguments: handle no-args error, parse each arg as float with optional suffix\n   - Suffix multipliers: s=1, m=60, h=3600, d=86400\n   - Sum all parsed durations, call time.Sleep\n   - Support \"infinity\"/\"inf\" as special case (sleep indefinitely)\n   - Exit 0 on success, exit 1 on errors with message to stderr\n\n   For `cmd/sleep/sleep_test.go`:\n   - TestDiff with BuildBinary and LookPath(\"gsleep\")\n   - DiffTest cases for: zero (0), fractional (0.01), with suffix (0.01s), multiple args (0 0), no args (ExitCode:1), invalid arg \"abc\" (ExitCode:1), negative arg \"-1\" (ExitCode:1)\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/sleep/main.go` and `cmd/sleep/sleep_test.go` in full, then compile and test. The task description says: \"Write all source files before running any build or test commands\" and the acceptance criteria require: AC1 (compiles), AC2 (go vet passes), AC3 (differential tests pass), AC4 (tests skip gracefully without gsleep). I was directly in the middle of implementing after reading the SRD — the next step is to create both files and verify them.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5413/07207fff-5b36-45b1-b434-af9af0cb9b66.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07207fff-5b36-45b1-b434-af9af0cb9b66","uuid":"cc9ebfd2-2867-4ba0-ac33-afa9237adf31","timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:57:01.226Z","isSynthetic":true}
