{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YXKUZuTZArxfm6tVogQDxM","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found the example files you need. Here are the key patterns from the existing implementations:\n\n## **1. Simple cmd/main.go (echo/main.go)**\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5413/cmd/echo/main.go`\n\n**Key patterns:**\n- **Copyright header format:**\n  ```go\n  // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n  // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n  ```\n\n- **Comment with spec reference:**\n  ```go\n  // Implements srd020-echo R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.3.\n  ```\n\n- **Import style:**\n  ```go\n  import (\n      \"os\"\n      \"strings\"\n      \n      \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n  )\n  ```\n\n- **SIGPIPE handler call:** First line in main()\n  ```go\n  func main() {\n      sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n      // ... rest of implementation\n  }\n  ```\n\n## **2. Test file pattern (echo_test.go)**\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5413/cmd/echo/echo_test.go`\n\n**Key patterns:**\n- **Differential testing setup:**\n  ```go\n  func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n      // Build the Go implementation\n      goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n      \n      // Get reference binary (GNU version with 'g' prefix, like 'gecho')\n      refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gecho\")\n      if err != nil {\n          t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n      }\n  ```\n\n- **Test struct array with DiffTest:**\n  ```go\n  tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n      {Name: \"no-args\", Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n      {Name: \"single-arg\", Args: []string{\"hello\"}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n      // Each test specifies Name, Args (optional), and Env\n  }\n  ```\n\n- **Running tests:**\n  ```go\n  testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n  ```\n\n**Test Structure:** Each test case has:\n- `Name`: Test case identifier\n- `Args`: Command-line arguments to pass\n- `Env`: Environment variables to set (typically `LC_ALL=C` for consistency)\n- Comments linking each test to specific requirements (R1.1, R1.2, etc.)\n\nThis differential testing pattern runs your implementation against the reference (GNU) binary and compares outputs to verify correctness."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07207fff-5b36-45b1-b434-af9af0cb9b66","uuid":"87bbf38c-577d-49d5-9c2a-68d697fde9eb","timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:57:23.782Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5413, find a few existing cmd/ implementations to understand the patterns used. I need to see:\n1. A simple cmd/ main.go that shows the copyright header format, import style, and how sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() is called\n2. A cmd/ test file that shows the differential testing pattern with testutils.BuildBinary and RunDiffTests\n\nLook at cmd/true/main.go or cmd/yes/main.go or cmd/echo/main.go for simple examples. Also look at their corresponding _test.go files. Show the full contents of one main.go and one test file.","agentId":"a6904ffe430cfbbb3","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found the example files you need. Here are the key patterns from the existing implementations:\n\n## **1. Simple cmd/main.go (echo/main.go)**\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5413/cmd/echo/main.go`\n\n**Key patterns:**\n- **Copyright header format:**\n  ```go\n  // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n  // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n  ```\n\n- **Comment with spec reference:**\n  ```go\n  // Implements srd020-echo R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.3.\n  ```\n\n- **Import style:**\n  ```go\n  import (\n      \"os\"\n      \"strings\"\n      \n      \"github.com/peta