{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012AvJEX85fsB8NZcB96apYg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The error cases fail because the stderr messages differ. I need to normalize the stderr for error cases. Let me look at how other tests handle this - I need to match the exact error format that gsleep uses, or use a normalizer.\n\nLooking at the differences:\n1. `no-args`: gsleep says `gsleep: missing operand\\nTry '/opt/homebrew/bin/gsleep --help' for more information.\\n` vs our `sleep: missing operand\\n`\n2. `invalid-arg`: gsleep uses single quotes `'abc'` vs our double quotes `\"abc\"`, and gsleep adds the Try line\n\n\n3. `negative-arg`: gsleep treats `-1` as an invalid option with a different error format entirely\n4. `empty-string`: similar quoting difference plus the Try line\n\nThe core issue is that our error messages don't match gsleep's format - we're missing the single quotes around arguments and the help suggestion line. Since the differential test framework compares stderr directly and we can't match the exact binary name in the error message, I should use a normalizer to strip out the binary-specific parts and standardize the quoting.\n\nLet me look for an existing NormalizeFunc I can use for this.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1130,"cache_read_input_tokens":36377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1130},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07207fff-5b36-45b1-b434-af9af0cb9b66","uuid":"6208dbbb-c26a-451e-a31b-fa76344d38c0"}
